('church-member-management-system',
 'Why Every Liberian Church Needs a Member Management System',
 'A member management system is the foundation of good church administration. This article explains what a member database should contain, how to keep it accurate, and how ChurchFlow helps Liberian churches maintain complete, privacy-compliant member records.',
 E'Your church members are your most important resource. Yet in most Liberian churches, the member database — if it exists at all — is a spiral notebook, an outdated Excel file, or a WhatsApp group that mixes real members with former attendees and the pastor''s family.\n\nA proper member management system changes everything.\n\n## What a Member Record Should Contain\n\nA complete member profile includes:\n\n- **Full name** — as the member prefers to be addressed\n- **Contact details** — phone number, WhatsApp, email (where applicable)\n- **Address** — neighbourhood or community in Liberia\n- **Date of birth** — for birthday follow-ups and age-based ministry placement\n- **Membership status** — visitor, new member, active member, transferred, inactive\n- **Baptism status** — baptised or not yet baptised\n- **Join date** — when they first became a member\n- **Department/ministry affiliation** — choir, ushers, youth ministry, etc.\n- **Emergency contact** — critical for pastoral care situations\n- **Notes** — pastoral observations, prayer needs, family situation\n\n## Why Accuracy Matters\n\nAn inaccurate member database is worse than no database at all — it creates false confidence. If your records show 400 members but 120 of them have left, moved, or died, every report and decision based on that data is wrong.\n\nSet a process: new members are added at registration, changes are updated within one week, inactive members are reviewed quarterly.\n\n## Privacy and Data Protection\n\nMember data is personal data. Your church has a responsibility to protect it. This means:\n\n- Only authorised staff can access member records\n- Data is not shared with third parties without consent\n- Members can request a copy of their data or ask for it to be deleted\n\nChurchFlow Liberia enforces these rules through role-based access control and GDPR-compliant data handling.\n\n## How ChurchFlow Manages Members\n\nChurchFlow gives each member a complete profile with all the fields above. Search and filter by any field. Export to CSV for reports. Track membership status over time. Assign members to departments and small groups.\n\nAll member data is stored securely on cloud infrastructure with daily backups.\n\n---\n\n*Build a complete, accurate member database for your church. Start with ChurchFlow Liberia.*',
 'Grace Kollie', 'Head of Product', 'Church Management',
 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1519817914152-22d216bb9170?w=1200&q=80',
 '6 min read', true, '2026-05-12 08:00:00+00'),

