('church-event-planning-liberia',
 'Church Event Planning in Liberia: From Sunday Service to Major Crusades',
 'Planning a successful church event — whether a Sunday service, midweek Bible study, or a city-wide crusade — requires coordination, communication, and careful record-keeping. This guide walks through the complete event planning process for Liberian churches.',
 E'From the weekly Sunday service to the annual church convention, events are the heartbeat of church life. But poorly planned events — where the PA system is not booked, the caterers show up late, or 200 people arrive expecting chairs for 80 — damage your church''s reputation and exhaust your volunteers.\n\nGood event planning is a discipline. Here is how to do it well.\n\n## The Event Planning Framework\n\n### 1. Define the event clearly\n\nBefore planning anything, answer these questions:\n- What is the purpose of this event?\n- Who is the target audience?\n- What does success look like?\n- What is the budget?\n\n### 2. Set the date and book the venue early\n\nFor major events, lock in the date at least 8 weeks in advance. Check against school holidays, public holidays, and other church events. If you are using an external venue, get a written booking confirmation.\n\n### 3. Build your team\n\nEvery event needs an event coordinator, a setup team, an AV/sound team, a hospitality/catering team, and an usher team. Assign names to each role — not just "someone from the youth department."\n\n### 4. Communicate in waves\n\n**8 weeks out:** Announce the event and date to the congregation.\n**4 weeks out:** Detailed information — theme, speakers, what to bring.\n**1 week out:** Final reminder with logistics.\n**Day before:** SMS reminder to all registered attendees.\n\n### 5. Plan for the worst\n\nWhat if it rains? What if the main speaker cancels? What if the generator fails? Great event planners have contingency plans for the three most likely things to go wrong.\n\n### 6. Debrief after every event\n\nWithin a week of the event, gather your team and answer honestly: What went well? What went poorly? What would we do differently? Document the answers so the next event is better.\n\n## Using ChurchFlow for Event Management\n\nChurchFlow Liberia''s events module lets you create events, set dates and locations, track RSVPs, and manage attendance. All event communication — announcements, reminders, follow-ups — can be sent via SMS directly from the platform.\n\n---\n\n*Plan better events with ChurchFlow Liberia. Try it free today.*',
 'Emmanuel Gbaye', 'Head of Engineering', 'Church Management',
 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1515187029135-18ee286d815b?w=1200&q=80',
 '7 min read', true, '2026-05-04 08:00:00+00'),

